# Build trees and fetched data. Corpora, papers, audio and page renders run to about
# 1.9 GB and every one of them is reproducible from the tools in this repository, so
# none of it is carried in git.
build/
build-*/

# The rendered site. mkdocs build writes it and the GitHub Action rebuilds it on every push, so a
# copy in git is one that goes stale the moment a page changes.
site/

# Cloned dependencies. MMgr used to sit here as four separate partial copies of itself, each one
# byte identical to the original and none of them recording which commit it came from, so a stale
# copy and a current one looked the same. `python tools/maintain/get_deps.py` clones it instead, and
# git in the clone answers what is checked out. Same rule as build/ and site/: what a tool can
# fetch is not carried here.
deps/

# The hand extractions and the papers they were read from. Every row is a form transcribed out of a
# published paper, so the tables are those papers' text and not this work's to redistribute, and the
# papers are their authors' copyright. Both live in a closed repository, inventoried by
# tools/maintain/corpus_manifest.py and signed there, and reach this tree under build/oracles and
# build/papers through tools/maintain/private_sync.py. The derivations built on them are this work's
# and stay in the repository: the ledger, the bound, the checks and the code are all here.
*.oracle.tsv

# Python caches. The tools here are run directly and cache next to themselves.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# What a LaTeX run leaves beside the source when it is not given an output directory.
#
# maint/texbuild/build_theory.sh compiles with -output-directory and leaves none of this. TeXworks
# and TeXShop compile IN PLACE, so a book opened in one of those to look at it comes back with a
# .pdf, a .log, a .toc, a .aux per included chapter and a synctex index. theory/anchor_sift picked
# up twelve such files that way, 705,688 bytes of it one synctex, and the arXiv packager copied
# every one of them into a submission before it learned to skip them.
#
# main.pdf is named rather than *.pdf on purpose. The corpus derivation chapter includes a
# matplotlib figure that is a PDF and belongs to the source.
*.aux
*.log
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.out
*.synctex
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
theory/*/main.pdf
theory/*/*/main.pdf
theory_bucket/*/main.pdf
theory_bucket/*/*/main.pdf

# Editor and OS leavings.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
